---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "This policy is a work in progress ahead of launch and will carry a dated version once finalized.";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Chick-Check collects, uses, and protects your data.">
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">{lastUpdated}</p>

		<p class="mt-6 text-slate-600">
			Chick-Check is a browser extension and account portal that warns you about phishing and scam links.
			This policy explains what data we collect, why, and what choices you have. Our starting principle:
			digital safety shouldn't require handing over more of your data than necessary — so we collect as
			little as we can, keep checks local wherever possible, and never sell your data or use it for
			advertising.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">What we collect</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">When you create an account, we store:</p>
		<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-600">
			<li>Your email address and a securely hashed version of your password (we never store your password in plain text).</li>
			<li>Your name, if you choose to provide one.</li>
			<li>Your feature settings — which protections (link scanning, form protection, typosquat warnings, download scanning, community reports, weekly email summary) you've switched on or off.</li>
			<li>Basic subscription/billing status (plan, status, and Stripe customer/subscription IDs) if you upgrade. Your actual payment details are handled entirely by Stripe — we never see or store your card information.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			To keep you signed in, we set a single authentication cookie (<code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">chick_check_session</code>).
			It's <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">httpOnly</code>, expires after 30 days, and is used only to
			recognize your session — not for tracking or advertising. We don't currently use analytics or
			advertising cookies.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">How link and page checks work</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			Chick-Check is designed to be local-first: as much detection as possible (blocklist matching,
			heuristics, on-device checks) happens directly in your browser, without sending the page you're
			visiting anywhere. Where a cloud lookup is needed, we send only a hashed prefix of the URL — not the
			full address or your browsing history — to reduce what leaves your device.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			For some checks, we rely on third-party threat-intelligence providers (for example, VirusTotal). Any
			such provider is covered by a data processing agreement, and we disclose here if a provider receives
			any data from a check.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Community reports</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			If you turn on community reports, sites you flag are anonymized before being added to the shared
			blocklist that protects other Chick-Check users. We don't attach your identity to a submitted report.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Who we share data with</h2>
		<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-600">
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> — processes payments for the optional Pro plan. See Stripe's own privacy policy for how they handle payment data.</li>
			<li><strong>Threat-intelligence providers</strong> (e.g. VirusTotal) — used for real-time link/file checks, under a data processing agreement.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Your rights</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">You can, at any time:</p>
		<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-600">
			<li>Review or change your account details and feature settings from your account dashboard.</li>
			<li>Request a copy of the data we hold about you.</li>
			<li>Delete your account and associated data.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			If you're in the EU/EEA, this includes the rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of
			processing, data portability, and objection under the GDPR. To exercise any of these, reach us via our
			<a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-brand-700 hover:underline">contact page</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Data retention</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			We keep account data for as long as your account is active. If you delete your account, we delete the
			associated data, other than what we're legally required to retain (for example, billing records).
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Children's privacy</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			Chick-Check is not directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect data from children without
			appropriate parental consent.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			We'll update this page as Chick-Check evolves and post a clear "last updated" date once the policy is
			finalized ahead of launch. Meaningful changes will be highlighted here.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Contact</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
			Questions about this policy or your data? Reach us via our
			<a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-brand-700 hover:underline">contact page</a>. Our legal
			entity details are listed in our
			<a href="/impressum" class="font-semibold text-brand-700 hover:underline">Impressum</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>
